933/1531, which would mislead an order-blind analysis; that confounder is explicitly controlled. High ambient volume (7,526 events) is also insufficient, since both endpoints are low-degree, triangle-free, and active in disjoint time bins."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**No genuine time-respecting cascade exists from 695 to 1495.**\n\nKey findings:\n\n1. **Direct test fails (step_01):** With the required \u2264600-unit gap, node 695 reaches only **2 nodes** total in the window \u2014 its forward temporal cone is essentially a dead end. 1495 is not among them.\n\n2. **The constraint is not the bottleneck (step_03, step_11):** Removing the max_wait limit entirely expands 695's reach to **588 nodes** \u2014 yet 1495 is *still* unreachable. So the failure is a genuine violation of temporal ordering, not merely an over-strict delay threshold. No path is enumerated at max_wait 600 or even 5000.\n\n3. **Static connectivity is a confounder, and it is ruled out (step_05, step_08):** Ignoring time, the two 2-hop neighborhoods overlap through hubs 274, 933 and 1531, so an order-blind analysis would wrongly suggest a connection. Time-respecting search rejects it.\n\n4. **Structural choke point (step_14, step_16):** 1495 has exactly **one inbound** edge, from 1517. Since influence must enter 1495 through 1517, and 1517 is itself unreachable from 695 under the delay budget, no cascade can terminate at 1495.\n\n5. **Volume/popularity confounders controlled (step_02, step_04, step_09, step_15):** The window is busy (7,526 events, 1,954 active nodes), but 695 and 1495 are low-degree (5 and 4 events, no repeats) and sit in **zero triangles**. Their sparse activity is also temporally misaligned (step_12), clustering in different bins. High ambient volume does not translate into a path.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Under the 600-unit gap constraint node 695 reaches only 2 nodes and never 1495; relaxing max_wait to unlimited expands reach to 588 nodes but still excludes 1495, so the failure is a true temporal-ordering violation rather than an artifact of the delay threshold. Node 1495 has a single inbound neighbour (1517), which is itself not temporally reachable from 695, forming a hard choke point. Static 2-hop neighbourhoods do overlap via hubs 274/933/1531, which would mislead an order-blind analysis; that confounder is explicitly controlled. High ambient volume (7,526 events) is also insufficient, since both endpoints are low-degree, triangle-free, and active in disjoint time bins.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 72422, "total_output_tokens": 4247, "total_tokens": 76669, "total_latency_ms": 67435, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}